In article <1992Jul8.170719.41403@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu> kuento@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu writes:
>(2) I've noticed that when I use a Wish to obtain an artifact, I don't
>seem to get one with its special properties intact: I wished for "a
>blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir" and *got* one, but it does not
>do any shock damage, ever, and I wished for "a blessed +3 long sword
>named Excalibur" and got one, but it does not defend me against level
>drains (as far as I can tell), and it most *certainly* does not
>"search" like a ring of searching does. Anyone who can explain to me
>what the problem is, or ways to consistently obtain *functional*
>artifacts? I mean, what Excalibur does for me, as far as I can tell,
>is nothing I couldn't do with *any* blessed +3 long sword, named or
>otherwise. This doesn't make any sense to me.

If you wish for such items properly and get them, they will work.  They don't
come out fake like the fake Amulets of Yendor you get if you wish for one of
those.

Excalibur doesn't provide searching, it only helps with the searching you
already have.

Mjollnir does produce shock damage, but there's no special message for it.
